Value port (.*)
Value total_bytes (.*)
Value total_frames (.*)
Value errors_rx (.*)
Value drops_tx (.*)
Value flow_ctrl (.*)

# Parse the output of "show interfaces" (port counters summary) on an HP
# AOS-S switch.
#
# Each data line looks like:
#   "  1          0              0              0            0            off"
# The "Flow" header wraps onto the line above the column headers, so the
# header and separator lines do not match and are ignored. One record per
# line; counters are comma-formatted.


Start
  ^\s+(?P<port>\d+)\s+(?P<total_bytes>[\d,]+)\s+(?P<total_frames>[\d,]+)\s+(?P<errors_rx>[\d,]+)\s+(?P<drops_tx>[\d,]+)\s+(?P<flow_ctrl>\S+)\s*$ -> Record
